The key calculation is subtler than a bare “constant versus conductor”: the plane-branch different inserts an exact contact compensator. For a pole branch \(\gamma\),
\[
\operatorname{ord}_\gamma F_\perp
=2\delta(\gamma)+m_\gamma-1+I_\gamma,
\]
where \(I_\gamma\) is its total intersection with the other local branches of the same projective fiber. Combining this with \(J=j\) and pole order \(3\) gives
\[
2\delta(\gamma)+I_\gamma=(d-3)m_\gamma+4,\qquad
\Delta_\gamma=3.
\]
At the filed branch this recovers the banked contact exactly:
\(4656=2388+2268=(168-3)42+4-2278\).
So there is an exact signed/contact bridge, but the contact term is precisely what prevents either terminal bound from controlling the other.
